{"source_commit": "fafc6b19d1e7f3bb80e3910c2650c2f3287ef86f", "source_run": "smoke31-1111-0039", "source_id": "G17", "law": "NRS-484B-127-3", "law_digest": "0780f8aca9bc464c", "occurrence": "NRS-484B-127-3@0780f8aca9bc464c:76-101", "span": "in a caravan or motorcade", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.procession_member` | a road user travelling as a member of an organized group of vehicles proceeding together in a column (a caravan, motorcade, convoy or procession), as the source labels the group; **group** attribute identifying the group, so that two road users are members of the same one **Not a stand-in for:** vehicles that merely follow one another in the same lane | general", "source_state": "proposed"}
{"source_commit": "fafc6b19d1e7f3bb80e3910c2650c2f3287ef86f", "source_run": "smoke31-1111-0039", "source_id": "G18", "law": "NRS-484B-297-6", "law_digest": "5a178d4df6df22d1", "occurrence": "NRS-484B-297-6@5a178d4df6df22d1:128-221", "span": "including, without limitation, a short section of the sidewalk that is missing or impassable,", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "st.impassable_section | a stretch of a sidewalk, or of the ground between a sidewalk and the roadway, that a pedestrian cannot traverse because its surface is missing or blocked, carried as a region with a boundary and the way it lies on; decides where a pedestrian may leave the sidewalk and where it may travel | general", "source_state": "proposed"}
{"source_commit": "fafc6b19d1e7f3bb80e3910c2650c2f3287ef86f", "source_run": "smoke31-1111-0039", "source_id": "G19", "law": "NRS-484B-270-3", "law_digest": "bcef26b221a13592", "occurrence": "NRS-484B-270-3@bcef26b221a13592:455-504", "span": "(b) When operating or parking a disabled vehicle;", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "ru.disabled | the vehicle cannot move under its own power (breakdown, damage, a flat tyre), as the source records it; decides whether a vehicle's presence or halt in a place is excused | general", "source_state": "proposed"}
{"source_commit": "fafc6b19d1e7f3bb80e3910c2650c2f3287ef86f", "source_run": "smoke31-1111-0039", "source_id": "G20", "law": "NRS-484B-270-3", "law_digest": "bcef26b221a13592", "occurrence": "NRS-484B-270-3@bcef26b221a13592:652-672", "span": "(f) In an emergency.", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "env.emergency | a sudden peril at the observation that a road user's conduct answers to (a fire, a medical emergency of an occupant, an imminent collision), as the source records it for that road user; decides whether a road user's presence in a place is excused | general", "source_state": "proposed"}
{"source_commit": "fafc6b19d1e7f3bb80e3910c2650c2f3287ef86f", "source_run": "smoke31-1111-0039", "source_id": "G21", "law": "NRS-484D-100-1", "law_digest": "230cefc3f0568ebc", "occurrence": "NRS-484D-100-1@230cefc3f0568ebc:558-618", "span": "and (c) When directed by an official traffic control device.", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`dev.lamps_on_sign` | a regulatory sign directing road users to display lighted lamps (headlamps on) where it governs, as at a tunnel or a daytime-headlamp section, with the same structured conditions attribute as dev.regulatory_sign (equivalently, a new catalogue code lamps_on of that atom) | general — it decides where the duty to display lighted lamps arises by day.", "source_state": "proposed"}
{"source_commit": "fafc6b19d1e7f3bb80e3910c2650c2f3287ef86f", "source_run": "smoke31-1111-0039", "source_id": "G22", "law": "NRS-484B-450-1c", "law_digest": "246833c41d20e47e", "occurrence": "NRS-484B-450-1c@246833c41d20e47e:109-134", "span": "or in compliance with law", "kind": "operator", "proposal": "An operator that decides whether, at an observation, some rule of the set that is engaged for the subject there is complied with only if the subject is halted (e.g. `Formula.haltRequired (subject)`): whether the halt is made 'in compliance with law'. The exception decides the action the law forbids, since it excuses a halt within an intersection whenever any law requires that halt (yielding to a responding emergency vehicle, to a pedestrian, to a school bus, and so on). The law names no rule, so no fixed composition carries it. The planned surrogate, 'an emergency vehicle with lamps or siren is in the scene', reads a road user that is tied neither to the subject nor to the intersection (gate UNANCHORED_VARIABLE). Anchoring it with rel.occupies, st.lane_enters, rel.surface_gap or a distance parameter would add conditions that the words 'in compliance with law' do not state, and it would still stand in for the law's requirement with a neighbouring atom.", "source_state": "proposed"}
